WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.720
What lies beyond the Star&nbsp;
Wars galaxy? Nobody knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.180
for sure — but Ahsoka might be about to show us.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.740
Ahsoka's fifth episode is quite the journey,&nbsp;
and it ends with the beginning of an even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.000
bigger one. After being knocked into the&nbsp;
sea by Baylan Skoll at the end of Episode 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.980
Ahsoka Tano finds herself in a mysterious&nbsp;
Force realm, where she comes face-to-face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.080
with her old master, Anakin Skywalker. As Hera&nbsp;
Syndulla searches the planet Seatos for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.520
Ahsoka revisits her tragic life story&nbsp;
through a series of Clone Wars flashbacks.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.640
"I'm teaching you how to lead, how to survive.&nbsp;
And to do that, you're going to have to fight."

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.280
Anakin pushes Ahsoka to her limits in the World&nbsp;
Between Worlds and even attacks her outright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.260
but it seems that his aggression is all a kind&nbsp;
of game — a way to help his old padawan find some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.120
peace within herself. And sure enough, Ahsoka&nbsp;
awakens from the ordeal with a powerful aura of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.880
serenity. She then quickly divines a way to pursue&nbsp;
Morgan Elsbeth, Sabine Wren, and the others, even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.160
without a star map. This is because Seatos is home&nbsp;
to a herd of purrgil, the hyperspace-traveling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.720
space whales that took Ezra Bridger and Grand&nbsp;
Admiral Thrawn away in Star Wars Rebels.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.120
At the end of Ahsoka Episode 5, Ahsoka uses the&nbsp;
Force to convince a purrgil through the Force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.320
to allow her and Huyang to dock their&nbsp;
ship in its mouth. Tucked away inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.520
they set off through hyperspace — and we already&nbsp;
have some clues as to where they might be going.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.860
As Ahsoka herself acknowledges to Huyang, she&nbsp;
has no idea whether or not the purrgil will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.420
actually take them to Sabine, Ezra, and Thrawn.&nbsp;
Because there are only three episodes left,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.240
the writers don't have much time&nbsp;
to play around in other places,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.740
but journeying through hyperspace isn't as&nbsp;
simple as hopping from point A to point B.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:42.120
Prior to Ahsoka, many believed that Thrawn&nbsp;
was simply hiding in some far corner of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.500
Unknown Regions, an uncharted sector of&nbsp;
the existing Star Wars galaxy. Notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.360
the ancient Sith planet of Exegol is located in&nbsp;
the Unknown Regions, along with the remnants of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.320
the Empire that would later become the Final&nbsp;
Order. If Ahsoka has to travel through that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.520
region of space on the way to Thrawn's galaxy, we&nbsp;
could get a glimpse of what's been going on there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.260
The Mandalorian Season 3 already established&nbsp;
that the Shadow Council of the Imperial Remnant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:09.060
is waiting for Thrawn's return, hiding in the&nbsp;
Unknown Regions until someone can bring him back.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.860
The Unknown Regions have barely been explored&nbsp;
in canonical Star Wars stories, which is fitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.120
given that they remain uncharted in-universe.&nbsp;
We know that Thrawn's species, the Chiss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:22.680
also hails from the area, and that it's quite&nbsp;
different from most known sectors of the galaxy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.900
But while the Unknown Regions are mysterious, even&nbsp;
less is known about what lies beyond them. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:32.460
Ahsoka's journey beyond the confines of the galaxy&nbsp;
opens up a number of exciting opportunities.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.740
In canon, Ahsoka is the first major Star Wars&nbsp;
story to voyage beyond the galaxy. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.640
the non-canon "Legends" timeline established&nbsp;
some details of what lies beyond the Outer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.840
Rim. Most famously, the Yuuzhan Vong&nbsp;
invaded from a neighboring galaxy in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.620
the EU's New Jedi Order laying waste to&nbsp;
beloved characters and whole planets.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.360
The Yuuzhan Vong were divisive at the time because&nbsp;
they felt like such an intense departure from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.680
usual tone and style of Star Wars, but that&nbsp;
doesn't mean we won't see some influence in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:03.900
whatever Ahsoka finds out there. It's also worth&nbsp;
noting that the canon Thrawn novels feature a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:07.860
race similar to the Yuuzhan Vong called the&nbsp;
Grysk. They're not quite as horrifying or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:12.480
dangerous as the classic "Legends" villains, and&nbsp;
they live in the Unknown Regions, not a separate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:17.520
galaxy. But there's a definite possibility that&nbsp;
Thrawn's presence in Ahsoka could lead to a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.660
version of the Yuuzhan Vong storyline,&nbsp;
one that places the Grysk in their stead.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.620
The implications that Ahsoka's story holds&nbsp;
for the greater Star Wars franchise are even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:30.180
more fascinating. Disney can't stay in&nbsp;
the Skywalker Saga forever. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.980
new stories will have to be told, and many of&nbsp;
them are likely to be completely divorced from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.420
existing Star Wars narrative. After all, that's&nbsp;
how you bring in new fans and keep the story going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:43.680
for younger generations. Because there's already&nbsp;
so much diversity in the main Star Wars galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.720
a new one might not sound like a huge deal.&nbsp;
But that's a galaxy with no Jedi; with no Sith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.880
Republic, or Empire. It's a huge pool of&nbsp;
possibilities just waiting to be tapped.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.120
"You've taken your first&nbsp;
step into a larger world."

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.960
All in all, Ahsoka's journey into the great beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.420
could be the start of big&nbsp;
new things for Star Wars.

